    "title": "Awesome-Selfhosted",
    "html": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted/master/_static/awesome.png\" alt=\"Awesome\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></a>   </p>\n<p>Self-hosting is the practice of hosting and managing applications on your own server(s) instead of consuming from <a href=\"https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/who-does-that-server-really-serve.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SaaSS</a> providers.</p>\n<p>This is a list of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_software\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Free</a> Software <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_service\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">network services</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_application\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">web applications</a> which can be hosted on your own server(s). Non-Free software is listed on the <a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted/blob/master/non-free.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Non-Free</a> page.</p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://awesome-selfhosted.net/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">HTML version</a> (recommended)</strong>, <a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Markdown version</a> (legacy).</p>\n<p>See <a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted#contributing\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Contributing</a>.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4>Table of contents</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted#software\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Software</a><ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-selfhosted/awesome-selfhosted#